summary: Upload the artifact-server qcow2 to AWS, deriving the URL inside Testing Farm

description: |
    Upload the qcow2 produced by a /image-mode/qcow2/build request to AWS as an
    AMI, reusing the testing-farm/tests ``/testing-farm/upload-qcow2``
    orchestration (``tft-admin``, inside the cnc image).

    Unlike running ``/testing-farm/upload-qcow2/aws`` directly, QCOW2_URL does not
    have to be supplied. The wrapper test /images/bootc-artifacts/upload-qcow2
    derives it from the build request *inside Testing Farm*, where the Red Hat ranch
    artifact server (``artifacts.osci.redhat.com``) is reachable, and then runs the
    upstream run.sh in the same shell. This lets the GitLab runner drive the upload
    with only the build request id, because the runner cannot resolve that host
    itself.

    Derivation and upload share one shell on purpose: the cnc container runs as a
    non-root user that cannot write tmt's work directory, so QCOW2_URL cannot be
    handed between tmt steps via $TMT_PLAN_ENVIRONMENT_FILE / $TMT_PLAN_SOURCE_SCRIPT
    (both live there). See upload-qcow2/upload.sh and README.adoc.

    Required variables:

      QCOW2_REQUEST ... The /image-mode/qcow2/build request id (or any string
                        containing it). Ignored if QCOW2_URL is set.

      IMAGE_NAME    ... Image name under which it is stored in the cloud.

      QCOW2_ARCH    ... Arch of the qcow2, passed to tft-admin.

    Optional variables:

      QCOW2_URL            ... Download URL of the qcow2. If set, it is used directly
                               and QCOW2_REQUEST is ignored.

      QCOW2_FILE           ... Name of the qcow2 file (default artifacts-bootc.qcow2,
                               matching the qcow2 build).

      TESTING_FARM_API_URL ... Testing Farm API holding the build request (defaults
                               to the public endpoint, which holds every request
                               regardless of ranch; the GET needs no token).

    Secret variables:

      VAULT_SECRET_ID ... Hashicorp Vault secret id for the cnc container. Pass as a
                          Testing Farm secret (``-s``).

environment:
  CLOUD: arr-aws
  QCOW2_FILE: artifacts-bootc.qcow2

discover:
  how: fmf
  test:
    - /images/bootc-artifacts/upload-qcow2

provision:
  how: container
  image: quay.io/testing-farm/cnc:latest
  user: cnc

execute:
  how: tmt
